    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d818">

                <pb facs="1011" n="887" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg887"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">422.11 G 93/1184: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hartman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-07-03T10:00:00-05:14"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3, 1921—10
                                a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 5—2:02 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>21. Department’s 6, June 28th, 5 p.m. I respectfully ask authority to defer
                    action on Department’s instruction pending the completion of negotiations now in
                    progress relating to the identical matters contained in Department’s telegram
                    between the President of Ecuador and the official management of Guayaquil and
                    Quito Railway Company here.</p>
                <p>I am informed that President has already agreed to transfer interest funds under
                    my care to credit of bondholders and only awaits proper document from G. Mills
                    and Company<anchor n="19" xml:id="d818-f1"/> which will protect the Minister of
                    Hacienda in making the transfer.</p>
                <p>I am further informed that satisfactory progress is being made in other matters
                    now under negotiation and it is feared that if action <pb facs="1012" n="888"
                        xml:id="pg888"/> on Department’s telegram is taken now it will result in
                    seriously embarrassing these negotiations.</p>
                <p>Full report of negotiations has been cabled New York office of railway by
                    management here. Please answer by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d818-f1" n="19" xml:id="d818-f1-content">
                <p>The banking firm of Glyn, Mills, Currie &amp; Co., London.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
